  "reasoning": "triage: program (a difference between two period balances), Type I (first question, single thread). preprocess: decomposed into the ending equity balance for 2010 (A) and the beginning equity balance for 2010 (B); the net change is the ending balance minus the beginning balance. retrieve: selected the rollforward rows 'balance end of year' (22974) and 'balance beginning of year' (19667) in the single 2010 column, rejecting the activity rows (net income, dividends declared, unrealized appreciation change, share repurchase, other movements) which are components rather than balances. reconcile: 19667 + 3108 - 443 + 742 - 303 + 203 = 22974, so the rollforward closes and the beginning balance ties to the prior year-end presentation. calculate: subtract(22974, 19667) = 3307. This also ties to the narrative statement that total shareholders' equity increased $3.3 billion in 2010.",
